{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles","id":1417430,"title":"How do Pantheons interpret Usurp/Sharing Mantles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-09T05:12:38-07:00","id":1417430,"title":"How do Pantheons interpret Usurp/Sharing Mantles?","content":"To those who had access to the Scion Demigod, how do you think the pantheons deal with Shared and, especially, usurped Mantles?<br /> <br /> Speaking from the Theoi perspective, which is the one I am more familiar with, it is hard to see they taking Usurping very well. They are a family first and foremost, and the idea of someone &quot;killing&quot; Zeus to take his place wouldn`t be taken well by the others if they are aware of it. Like, is Hera okay sleeping with a man who killed her previous husband and took his place and name? Is Ares not wanting revenge for his father`s murder?<br /> <br /> The only way I see it working is as if they are unaware of it, like when someone takes a Mantle all minds are changed so now he is that deity, and has always being. If so, how this works for the player, who knows he wasn`t Zeus last week, but now everybody treat as if he always was.<br /> <br /> This is all not counting what they consider happened? Do they think a Demigod just faced Zeus and lost? If so, why would they allow any of their Scions to ever try, as they can never win? And even if they have some notion, how would the Scions even be aware they can do it? Beyond more weird Scions who are willing to stole identities of deities, I can`t imagine Scions in the World being aware that it is even a possibility.<br /> <br /> Sharing Mantles seen like a more natural identity, as you can be a shared but still yourself. The book points Phobos and Deimos, who seen to be their own beings while being a sharing Mantles. You are just in direct connection to the Major god and somewhat seen as the same, not outright taking their place.<br /> <br /> Same goes for what I know of the Aesir, honestly, but they would have a better acceptance of something taking at least the name of Odin, if for no other reason but to keep Ragnaroc as it is.<br /> <br /> While the book does comment about other deities of other pantheons, I am too uneducated on them to comment, so I will let others better equipped to do so.<br /> <br /> So, how do you guys consider the pantheons on your games deal with it?<br /> <br /> Thank you all very much for the help and attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T08:45:58-07:00","id":1417456,"title":"","content":"I'm not an expert on anything but from what little I know... Like, the Deva would be ALL ABOUT Sharing and Merging Mantles.<br /> <br /> Like &quot;Oh snap I realized I was Shiva all along&quot; happens quite often in their legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T08:55:24-07:00","id":1417458,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s said in the manuscript that to mortals at least, when (for example) some Scion usurps Thor\u2019s Mantle, all the mortals see regardless who wins, is Thor winning another fight as the winner becomes retroactively always having been Thor, for Gods we don\u2019t fully know yet how they feel but from what we know it seems like Gods will both remember the previous Thor while also remembering you as always being Thor doing all the Thor things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:36:48-07:00","id":1417468,"title":"","content":"Well, in the Brigitte Fiction, the other Scion understand that Baronne Brigitte is actually Brigitte and she never knew that Orisha symbols, while the devotes have, so Legendary creatures may be immune to the re-created myth as they are part of the myth itself.<br /> <br /> I think the gods (and heroes and demigods) would notice the change, and probably would be capable of recognize the defeated god (what ever is the leftovers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:38:23-07:00","id":1417469,"title":"","content":"This one has me confused too tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T12:49:38-07:00","id":1417478,"title":"","content":"I figure a lot more of these questions will be answered come the God book. But Gods seem to be very much aware of Mantles and the inheriting thereof, such as when the first chapter mentions that Ares and Thor may well be readying their kids to be their replacements.<br /> <br /> And it's possible that some Gods may have a stance of &quot;Well you weren't as good a Thor as the new guy otherwise you'd still be Thor&quot;. We really have no idea how these kinds of things are viewed from the perspective of the Gods.<br /> <br /> I'd take it piece by piece, for the sake of a story. A Demigod doesn't necessarily need to know what everyone thinks of them trying to become the new Zeus. Most will probably defend Zeus because he's Zeus, but once the new guy becomes Zeus, well that's Zeus now isn't it?<br /> <br /> (Though some may track down the one who was Zeus but isn't any more and try to coax them to the path of becoming the New New Zeus, because they liked that Zeus more than this new Zeus. Or some may like this new Zeus better than the old one)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417468#post1417468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in the Brigitte Fiction, the other Scion understand that Baronne Brigitte is actually Brigitte and she never knew that Orisha symbols, while the devotes have, so Legendary creatures may be immune to the re-created myth as they are part of the myth itself.<br /> <br /> I think the gods (and heroes and demigods) would notice the change, and probably would be capable of recognize the defeated god (what ever is the leftovers).</div> </div> </div> </div>While a possible read, I figure that the reason why she didn't know Baronne Brigitte's symbol was because she, uh, wasn't a worshipper of the Loa and you can't expect someone to recognize EVERY symbol for EVERY Loa. There's a lot of Loa.<br /> <br /> However, I do think she connected the dots... BUT not because she's a Hero and they have some ripple proof memory. I think it was because Omolara was Brigitte's friend, and remembers talking to her like a month ago. Just &quot;BARONNE Brigitte? I knew a Brigitte and <i>ooooooh</i>. Heh. Guess she did it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-09-2020, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T14:51:41-07:00","id":1417487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417478#post1417478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure a lot more of these questions will be answered come the God book. But Gods seem to be very much aware of Mantles and the inheriting thereof, such as when the first chapter mentions that Ares and Thor may well be readying their kids to be their replacements.<br /> <br /> And it's possible that some Gods may have a stance of &amp;quot;Well you weren't as good a Thor as the new guy otherwise you'd still be Thor&amp;quot;. We really have no idea how these kinds of things are viewed from the perspective of the Gods.<br /> <br /> I'd take it piece by piece, for the sake of a story. A Demigod doesn't necessarily need to know what everyone thinks of them trying to become the new Zeus. Most will probably defend Zeus because he's Zeus, but once the new guy becomes Zeus, well that's Zeus now isn't it?<br /> <br /> (Though some may track down the one who was Zeus but isn't any more and try to coax them to the path of becoming the New New Zeus, because they liked that Zeus more than this new Zeus. Or some may like this new Zeus better than the old one)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While a possible read, I figure that the reason why she didn't know Baronne Brigitte's symbol was because she, uh, wasn't a worshipper of the Loa and you can't expect someone to recognize EVERY symbol for EVERY Loa. There's a lot of Loa.<br /> <br /> However, I do think she connected the dots... BUT not because she's a Hero and they have some ripple proof memory. I think it was because Omolara was Brigitte's friend, and remembers talking to her like a month ago. Just &amp;quot;BARONNE Brigitte? I knew a Brigitte and <i>ooooooh</i>. Heh. Guess she did it.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense when you put it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T17:13:19-07:00","id":1417497,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417478#post1417478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Though some may track down the one who was Zeus but isn't any more and try to coax them to the path of becoming the New New Zeus, because they liked that Zeus more than this new Zeus. Or some may like this new Zeus better than the old one).</div> </div> </div> </div>Before I say anything else, this idea is rad. The idea of the Ancient Gods losing their Mantles and needing to fight their way back to the top of the food chain is awesome. Like, go to the players and go &quot;you all, choose some Greek Gods. You gonna play them now, from the ground up&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417478#post1417478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure a lot more of these questions will be answered come the God book. But Gods seem to be very much aware of Mantles and the inheriting thereof, such as when the first chapter mentions that Ares and Thor may well be readying their kids to be their replacements.<br /> <br /> And it's possible that some Gods may have a stance of &quot;Well you weren't as good a Thor as the new guy otherwise you'd still be Thor&quot;. We really have no idea how these kinds of things are viewed from the perspective of the Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that they seem to be aware, and the book considers as such, but if so, the implication is that they don`t really care about who is each god as long as someone is? I mean, Thor has a very good reason to be training a successor, but again, does Hera does not care about who her husband is as long as he has the Mantle of Zeus? Do the gods only interact and only care through their Mantles?<br /> <br /> Unless said otherwise, especially considering their relations mimic family, social and professional relations, they do work the same. Focusing on Zeus, he cares about his sons and daughters and acts as a (very bad) husband to Hera. When someone takes his mantle, do Hera is now married to someone she might not even know (I mean the Hera behind the Mantle)? Do their sons care about the new Zeus equally just because he now has the Mantle?<br /> <br /> Yes, it might be some important piece of understanding missing that will be on the God book, but so far those are questions I think are important to ask, at least so I can understand how the gods deal with it. Like, would they even help someone kill and usurp the identity of their relatives? This is important to know because if a Scion of Apolo decides to become the New Zeus 2.0, how would the gods react to it? Would they consider this beyond just a blasphemy, a horrendous act towards his own Grandfather and their close relative? Or would they be like &quot;I hope you can do it, the previous one is a cheating piece of crap.&quot; and help if their interests align with the new Zeus?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417478#post1417478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd take it piece by piece, for the sake of a story. A Demigod doesn't necessarily need to know what everyone thinks of them trying to become the new Zeus. Most will probably defend Zeus because he's Zeus, but once the new guy becomes Zeus, well that's Zeus now isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, they shouldn't know what they all want, but I need to consider how they would act when presented with this possibility. And how would even the Demigods come with this idea? For us, it makes sense on the meta-game, but in-game I don't think someone would think &quot;I can become the New Zeus&quot;, as from their point of view in the mythology it isn`t even a possibility. You can dethrone him, you can imprison him, you can trick or coerce him to be different or give you the power. But <i>become him </i>is simply impossible.<br /> <br /> And would the gods even discuss this topic with them? Like, a Demigod is all sad and so on with Zeus` attitudes, and them Athena come to them and tell that if they work hard enough, they can become a better Zeus? I mean, I love the surrealism of this Scene, but I just want to know if it is supposed to be the case in-game.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, wouldn`t be this topic a very dangerous one to bring up, as the more Scions who know this is a possibility, the more they risk having Scions trying to do so and killing them?<br /> <br /> Again, I am thinking mostly through the Theoi lens, which is the one I am most educated on, and I am honestly interested in knowing what would other pantheons consider about it.<br /> <br /> Also, I apologize if I am overthinking about it. It just that I am running a game with Scions about to reach Legend 4, when they should start considering such questions, and I don`t know how to introduce it to them. Would the gods be aware? Would they talk about it? Would they be okay knowing their own blood plans to kill their relatives? Are the Mantles so much more important than those behind it that, as long it is someone there to be a Zeus, they don`t care who is it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T18:50:20-07:00","id":1417501,"title":"","content":"I think that viewing the mantle and the identity of a god as separate things are a viewpoint that is lost once a mortal scion reaches apotheosis and lose their mortality.<br /> <br /> The gods are not likely to even think in terms of old zeus and new zeus.<br /> Zeus is Zeus. The mantle is the god.<br /> If a scion reaching apotheosis usurp Zeus mantle then, from other gods perspectives, its not consodered much different than growing up after learning something new.<br /> <br /> All that to say that this is the angle i intend to use in my own games because i find it helps to showcase the difference that a scion goes through when they become a god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T19:34:53-07:00","id":1417502,"title":"","content":"Shared mantle has the easiest interpretation to me. Like the Theoi have had instances of that and would view it as sibling putting on the different hats for the job. You know like visiting a friend or relative at work and seeing the aspects of their personality that are necessary to emphasize, display, or suppress to function in their duties. Just since the gods are able to be manifest in multiple places you also occasionally get instances of work relation sharing a drink with off duty relation.<br /> <br /> As for usurpation, I feel like there are certain aspects that are just considered part of the job. So someone usurps Zeus or Hera then being the other one's spouse is just part and parcel the deal and the others deal with that. Probably followed by some form of reintroduction between the new bearer and the other members of the pantheon like this was some sort utterly absurd self-improvement program.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T21:09:25-07:00","id":1417510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417497#post1417497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but again, does Hera does not care about who her husband is as long as he has the Mantle of Zeus? Do the gods only interact and only care through their Mantles?<br /> <br /> Unless said otherwise, especially considering their relations mimic family, social and professional relations, they do work the same. Focusing on Zeus, he cares about his sons and daughters and acts as a (very bad) husband to Hera. When someone takes his mantle, do Hera is now married to someone she might not even know (I mean the Hera behind the Mantle)? Do their sons care about the new Zeus equally just because he now has the Mantle?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this would explain a lot about Zeus and Hera's relationship, if Hera was Fatebound to be the wife of this guy who replaced the man she really loved, and Zeus wasn't actually interested in this lady-who-is-his-older-sister but was Fatebound to have married her, and so took basically any excuse he could to go womanizing.<br /> <br /> I don't know the answer to your question, but I think it's probably relevant that all the Gods were, by canon, previously Scions themselves and ascended somehow. It might be possible to posit that, yeah, these Mantles are in a familial relationship, but the original Scions weren't. After all, a lot of the Greek familiality comes from an insistence that existence came in a series of couplings with Chaos birthing Night and Night birthing Earth and Earth birthing Time and Time birthing Zeus: it wouldn't be hard to say that that was something thrust upon the pantheon by Fate, rather than an actual familial connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T21:31:57-07:00","id":1417512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417497#post1417497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Before I say anything else, this idea is rad. The idea of the Ancient Gods losing their Mantles and needing to fight their way back to the top of the food chain is awesome. Like, go to the players and go &amp;quot;you all, choose some Greek Gods. You gonna play them now, from the ground up&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I definitely agree that they seem to be aware, and the book considers as such, but if so, the implication is that they don`t really care about who is each god as long as someone is? I mean, Thor has a very good reason to be training a successor, but again, does Hera does not care about who her husband is as long as he has the Mantle of Zeus? Do the gods only interact and only care through their Mantles?<br /> <br /> Unless said otherwise, especially considering their relations mimic family, social and professional relations, they do work the same. Focusing on Zeus, he cares about his sons and daughters and acts as a (very bad) husband to Hera. When someone takes his mantle, do Hera is now married to someone she might not even know (I mean the Hera behind the Mantle)? Do their sons care about the new Zeus equally just because he now has the Mantle?<br /> <br /> Yes, it might be some important piece of understanding missing that will be on the God book, but so far those are questions I think are important to ask, at least so I can understand how the gods deal with it. Like, would they even help someone kill and usurp the identity of their relatives? This is important to know because if a Scion of Apolo decides to become the New Zeus 2.0, how would the gods react to it? Would they consider this beyond just a blasphemy, a horrendous act towards his own Grandfather and their close relative? Or would they be like &amp;quot;I hope you can do it, the previous one is a cheating piece of crap.&amp;quot; and help if their interests align with the new Zeus?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree, they shouldn't know what they all want, but I need to consider how they would act when presented with this possibility. And how would even the Demigods come with this idea? For us, it makes sense on the meta-game, but in-game I don't think someone would think &amp;quot;I can become the New Zeus&amp;quot;, as from their point of view in the mythology it isn`t even a possibility. You can dethrone him, you can imprison him, you can trick or coerce him to be different or give you the power. But <i>become him </i>is simply impossible.<br /> <br /> And would the gods even discuss this topic with them? Like, a Demigod is all sad and so on with Zeus` attitudes, and them Athena come to them and tell that if they work hard enough, they can become a better Zeus? I mean, I love the surrealism of this Scene, but I just want to know if it is supposed to be the case in-game.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, wouldn`t be this topic a very dangerous one to bring up, as the more Scions who know this is a possibility, the more they risk having Scions trying to do so and killing them?<br /> <br /> Again, I am thinking mostly through the Theoi lens, which is the one I am most educated on, and I am honestly interested in knowing what would other pantheons consider about it.<br /> <br /> Also, I apologize if I am overthinking about it. It just that I am running a game with Scions about to reach Legend 4, when they should start considering such questions, and I don`t know how to introduce it to them. Would the gods be aware? Would they talk about it? Would they be okay knowing their own blood plans to kill their relatives? Are the Mantles so much more important than those behind it that, as long it is someone there to be a Zeus, they don`t care who is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally Liked this post. And yeah, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> that Fatebinding probably plays a big part in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T17:45:40-07:00","id":1417577,"title":"","content":"What if lower ranking gods that share a mantle are clients (let's use the medieval term client in fife) of the higher ranking god? Take Zeus of the Agora: a divine patron of democracy. He could easily be a client in fife to Zeus Lord of Justice. And Zeus Lord of Justice would be a client in fife to He of Ditka (the earliest known form of Zeus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T17:51:52-07:00","id":1417578,"title":"","content":"Ehh, the way Mantles are described they\u2019re more like alternate personalities or versions of the same god","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T04:12:02-07:00","id":1417616,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24769_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24769\" data-vbnamecard=\"24769\">Magicjohnny</a>. I think that\u2019s a better model for how Mantles work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:39:09-07:00","id":1417669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417430-how-do-pantheons-interpret-usurp-sharing-mantles?p=1417578#post1417578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehh, the way Mantles are described they\u2019re more like alternate personalities or versions of the same god</div> </div> </div> </div>But is it the only playable model for how mantles work. Or even the only model for how mantles work that fits mythology. It seems to me different pantheons would do it in different ways. Heck some pantheons might allow/prefer handling mantles in multiple different ways. But let's enjoy our own games and go our own ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T13:19:41-07:00","id":1417692,"title":"","content":"Different pantheons treat them differently yes I agree, but for the Theoi, the various different Mantles are more like focused versions of the same being, all the different mantles of Zeus are Zeus just more specialized approaches of him so to say, from what I know of ancient Hellenism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}